EXAM_DATA.papers["2000"] = {"id":"2000","year":2000,"label":"2000 旧卷","era":"old","sourceUrl":"https://english-exam.lazynote.cn/kaoyan/paper/2000/","timeLimitMin":180,"scoreMode":"raw","parts":[{"id":"section1","kind":"cloze","title":"Section I 完形填空","directions":"Directions: For each numbered blank in the following passage, there are four choices marked ［A］, ［B］, ［C］and ［D］. Choose the best one and mark your answer on ANSWER SHEET 1 by blackening the corresponding letter in the brackets with a pencil. (10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section1-1","text":"If a farmer wishes to succeed, he must try to keep a wide gap between his consumption and his production. He must store a large quantity of grain   {{1}}   consuming all his grain immediately. He can continue to support himself and his family   {{2}}   he produces a surplus. He must use this surplus in three ways: as seed for sowing, as an insurance   {{3}}   the unpredictable effects of bad weather and as a commodity which he must sell in order to   {{4}}   old agricultural implements and obtain chemical fertilizers to   {{5}}   the soil. He may also need money to construct irrigation   {{6}}   and improve his farm in other ways. If no surplus is available, a farmer cannot be   {{7}}   . He must either sell some of his property or   {{8}}   extra funds in the form of loans. Naturally he will try to borrow money at a low   {{9}}   of interest, but loans of this kind are not   {{10}}   obtainable."}]},"questions":[{"n":1,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"other than"},{"key":"B","text":"as well as"},{"key":"C","text":"instead of"},{"key":"D","text":"more than"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"1.","reason":"“储存大量粮食”与“立刻全部吃掉”天然对立 本句是 He must store a large quantity of grain __(1)__ consuming all his grain immediately. 前半句“储存大量粮食”和后半句“立刻把粮食全部吃掉”是非此即彼的对立关系,与开篇 keep a wide gap between his consumption and his production 也呼应,空格须填“而不是”这一替代关系。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"other than通常用于否定句或表“除了”,如 nothing other than…,与本句“储存而非吃掉”的替代关系不符。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"as well as意为“以及、也”,若选此,则等于说“既要储存又要立刻吃掉”,自相矛盾,且违背 keep a wide gap between his consumption and his production 的主旨。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"instead of 把“储存大量粮食”与“立刻全部吃掉”这两个相反动作连接成替代关系,与主旨一致,代入后整句通顺。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"more than表示“多于、不仅仅”,本句两侧并非数量比较或递进,选它则句意失焦。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":2,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"only if"},{"key":"B","text":"much as"},{"key":"C","text":"long before"},{"key":"D","text":"ever since"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"2.","reason":"“继续养家”依赖“有盈余”这一前提 本句 He can continue to support himself and his family __(2)__ he produces a surplus. 主句是“能继续养活自己和家人”,从句是“产出余粮”,前者完全依赖后者——“只有产出余粮,才能维持”,正是条件关系,与文章主旨 surplus 是命脉相吻合。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"only if强调“产出余粮”是“能继续养家”的唯一必要条件,与上下文“没有余粮就不能 self-sufficient”形成正反呼应。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"much as意为“尽管、虽然”,需要主从句之间存在让步关系,但本句两半是“依赖”而非“尽管…仍然”,逻辑不合。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"long before表“在…之前很久”,原文未涉及时间先后,选它会让句子变成“在他产生余粮之前很久就能养家”,与文意相反。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"ever since需要明确的过去起点,与文中讨论的是一般规律不符,逻辑指向也不是条件而是时间。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":3,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"for"},{"key":"B","text":"against"},{"key":"C","text":"of"},{"key":"D","text":"towards"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"3.","reason":"“保险”要对抗的是“恶劣天气的不可预料后果” 本句的余粮第二用途 as an insurance __(3)__ the unpredictable effects of bad weather,insurance 防的对象是“不可预知的坏天气后果”,语义上是对抗关系。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"insurance for sb. 多指“为某人投保”,但接“不可预测的天气后果”不通,且无法表达“防”这一关键语义。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"against与 insurance 构成“防范……”的固定搭配,精准对应“防恶劣天气”这一语义,代入即通。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"of虽然可以接 insurance 表所属,但无法表达“防范坏天气后果”这一动作意味,语义层次浅。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"towards表方向或态度,如 attitude towards,与 insurance 不构成自然搭配。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":4,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"replace"},{"key":"B","text":"purchase"},{"key":"C","text":"supplement"},{"key":"D","text":"dispose"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"4.","reason":"“卖余粮换钱”是为了“处理旧农具并买化肥” 本句 as a commodity which he must sell in order to __(4)__ old agricultural implements and obtain chemical fertilizers to __(5)__ the soil.,卖粮所得有两个用途:对旧农具做某事、并 obtain(获得)化肥;空 (4) 与 obtain 并列,作用对象是“旧的”农具,常识是“以新换旧”。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"replace意为“用新的代替旧的”,与 old agricultural implements 完美对应,且与并列动作 obtain chemical fertilizers(获得新化肥)构成“以新换旧+添新物”的工整结构。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"purchase义为购买,但“购买旧农具”与文意“改善生产”相反——一个力图致富的农民理应换新而非买旧。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"supplement意为补充、增补,常用于资源/营养/收入,搭配“旧农具”不通——补充旧农具既不解决问题,也不符合句意。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"dispose表“处理、处置”需接 of(dispose of),本身无“换新”的语义,即便忽略搭配也只表示“扔掉”,跟下文“买化肥改良土壤”不形成对照。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":5,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"enhance"},{"key":"B","text":"mix"},{"key":"C","text":"feed"},{"key":"D","text":"raise"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"5.","reason":"化肥之于土壤=“喂养”土壤 原文 obtain chemical fertilizers to __(5)__ the soil,化肥(fertilizer)对土壤的作用,英语习惯说 feed the soil——“给土壤喂养养分”,这是英语农学语境的固定意象。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"enhance多接抽象事物(reputation, ability, performance),enhance the soil 不是地道搭配,语义偏抽象。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"mix表混合,要求 mix A with B 结构,直接 mix the soil 语义残缺,且不能表达“施肥养土”的因果。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"feed在农学语境中常与 soil 搭配,意为“给土壤补给养分”,fertilizer feeds the soil 是地道说法,符合“买化肥→喂土壤→改良地力”的逻辑链。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"raise可表“提高/饲养/筹集”,但 raise the soil 既不指地力,也不指土壤被抬高,语义不合。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":6,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"vessels"},{"key":"B","text":"routes"},{"key":"C","text":"paths"},{"key":"D","text":"channels"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"6.","reason":"irrigation channels=灌溉水渠,专有搭配 原文 He may also need money to construct irrigation __(6)__ and improve his farm in other ways.,irrigation(灌溉)与 channels 构成固定农业术语“灌溉渠道”,这是地道英语。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"vessels指轮船、容器或血管,虽然 blood vessels 极常用,但与 irrigation 搭配不通,construct vessels 也不指挖水渠。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"routes多指交通路线、运输线,与 construct(建造)搭配也偏奇怪,不是灌溉惯用术语。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"paths指人或动物走的小路,不指水流通道,与“灌溉”无关。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"channels本义“沟渠/水道”,与 irrigation 构成专业术语“灌溉渠”,construct irrigation channels 是地道动作,代入即通。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":7,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"self-confident"},{"key":"B","text":"self-sufficient"},{"key":"C","text":"self-satisfied"},{"key":"D","text":"self-restrained"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"7.","reason":"“没有余粮就不能自给”是文章核心断言 本句 If no surplus is available, a farmer cannot be __(7)__. 与前句 He can continue to support himself and his family __(2)__ he produces a surplus. 正反对应:有余粮才能养家;没余粮就不能“自足/自给”——这是文章关于 surplus 的核心命题。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"self-confident指心理上的自信,与“是否有余粮维持生计”不是同一维度,属偷换概念。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"self-sufficient意为“自给自足”,直接与前句 He can continue to support himself and his family 对偶——有余则自足,无余则不能自足,逻辑严丝合缝。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"self-satisfied含贬义“自我满足”,与“能否维持生计”这一物质命题方向不一致,且通常用于个体心态,不用于经济独立性。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"self-restrained指克制欲望,与“有无余粮决定生计”毫无逻辑联系。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":8,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"search"},{"key":"B","text":"save"},{"key":"C","text":"offer"},{"key":"D","text":"seek"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"8.","reason":"“需要钱→寻找额外资金=贷款”,语义自然 本句 He must either sell some of his property or __(8)__ extra funds in the form of loans. 给出两条出路:卖资产或“以贷款形式获取额外资金”;空格动词的语义应当是“去寻求/获取”,而非“搜查/储存/提供”。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"search做及物动词意为“搜查(人/地)”,如 search the house;若表“寻找资金”需 search for,直接 search extra funds 搭配错误。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"save意为“储存、节省”,但下文 in the form of loans(以贷款形式)明示是借入,不是存,逻辑相反。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"offer指主语主动给出,而农民是资金接收方,选它会把借贷方向颠倒。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"seek意为“寻求”,seek funds/seek loans 是地道搭配,与“以贷款形式获取额外资金”的语义完全契合。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":9,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"proportion"},{"key":"B","text":"percentage"},{"key":"C","text":"rate"},{"key":"D","text":"ratio"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"9.","reason":"interest rate=利率,经济学固定术语 本句 Naturally he will try to borrow money at a low __(9)__ of interest, but loans of this kind are not __(10)__ obtainable.,a low rate of interest = a low interest rate(低利率)是经济学约定表达。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"proportion强调“部分与整体之比”,如 a large proportion of,与 interest 不构成术语。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"percentage强调以百分数表达的比率,如 a percentage of 5%,但 a low percentage of interest 不是行内表达,术语固定为 interest rate。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"rate与 interest 构成经济学固定术语“利率”,a low rate of interest 即“低利率”,精确地道。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"ratio指两个量之间的比值,如 a ratio of 2:1,与单一变量“利息率”不匹配。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":10,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"genuinely"},{"key":"B","text":"obviously"},{"key":"C","text":"presumably"},{"key":"D","text":"frequently"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"10.","reason":"but 转折:低息贷款“不常见”才符合现实 本句 Naturally he will try to borrow money at a low __(9)__ of interest, but loans of this kind are not __(10)__ obtainable.,but 暗示“虽然想低息,但现实并非如此”——“低息贷款并非经常能得到”,与文末“无奈现实”的语气一致。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"genuinely强调真实性(如 genuinely happy),not genuinely obtainable 读起来像“并非真正可得”,语义勉强且过度推断。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"obviously意为显而易见,若说“低息贷款显然不可得”,口吻过于绝对,且与 Naturally he will try 形成的“合理愿望”不是同一层次的对比。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"presumably含说话人推测口吻,但本句陈述客观事实“低息贷款常常拿不到”,无须推测语气。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"frequently意为“频繁、经常”,not frequently obtainable=“并不经常能得到”,正好回应农民想要低息但现实难求的窘境,与 but 的转折语义对位。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-1","kind":"reading","title":"Text 1","textNo":1,"directions":"Directions: Each of the passages below is followed by some questions. For each question there are four answers marked ［A］, ［B］, ［C］and ［D］. Read the passages carefully and choose the best answer to each of the questions. Then mark your answer on ANSWER SHEET 1 by blackening the corresponding letter in the brackets with a pencil. (40 points)","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 1","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-1","text":"A history of long and effortless success can be a dreadful handicap, but, if properly handled, it may become a driving force. When the United States entered just such a glowing period after the end of the Second World War, it had a market eight times larger than any competitor, giving its industries unparalleled economies of scale. Its scientists were the world's best; its workers the most skilled. America and Americans were prosperous beyond the dreams of the Europeans and Asians whose economies the war had destroyed."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-2","text":"It was inevitable that this primacy should have narrowed as other countries grew richer. Just as inevitably, the retreat from predominance proved painful. By the mid-1980s Americans had found themselves at a loss over their fading industrial competitiveness. Some huge American industries, such as consumer electronics, had shrunk or vanished in the face of foreign competition. By 1987 there was only one American television maker left, Zenith. (Now there is none: Zenith was bought by South Korea's LG Electronics in July.) Foreign-made cars and textiles were sweeping into the domestic market. America's machine-tool industry was on the ropes. For a while it looked as though the making of semiconductors, which America had invented and which sat at the heart of the new computer age, was going to be the next casualty."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-3","text":"All of this caused a crisis of confidence. Americans stopped taking prosperity for granted. They began to believe that their way of doing business was failing, and that their incomes would therefore shortly begin to fall as well. The mid-1980s brought one inquiry after another into the causes of America's industrial decline. Their sometimes sensational findings were filled with warnings about the growing competition from overseas."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-4","text":"How things have changed! In 1995 the United States can look back on five years of solid growth while Japan has been struggling. Few Americans attribute this solely to such obvious causes as a devalued dollar or the turning of the business cycle. Self-doubt has yielded to blind pride. \"American industry has changed its structure, has gone on a diet, has learnt to be more quick-witted,\" according to Richard Cavanagh, executive dean of Harvard's Kennedy School of Government. \"It makes me proud to be an American just to see how our businesses are improving their productivity,\" says Stephen Moore of the Cato Institute, a think-tank in Washington, DC. And William Sahlman of the Harvard Business School believes that people will look back on this period as \"a golden age of business management in the United States.\""}]},"questions":[{"n":11,"stem":"The U.S. achieved its predominance after World War II because____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"it had made painstaking efforts towards this goal"},{"key":"B","text":"its domestic market was eight times larger than before"},{"key":"C","text":"the war had destroyed the economies of most potential competitors"},{"key":"D","text":"the unparalleled size of its workforce had given an impetus to its economy"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"美国在第二次世界大战后取得主导地位是因为____。","choicesZh":{"A":"它为实现这一目标付出了艰苦的努力","B":"其国内市场比以前扩大了八倍","C":"战争摧毁了大多数潜在竞争对手的经济","D":"其劳动力规模无可比拟,为经济发展提供了推动力"},"analysis":{"type":"题干以 because 句末待补全的结构出现，要求从四个选项里选出符合文意的原因。本质是问文章对某事实成因的具体陈述。","parse":"题干 The U.S. achieved its predominance after World War II because____ 是不完整陈述句，主干 The U.S. achieved its predominance；after World War II 是时间状语；because 后接四个选项作原因状语从句。结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"America and Americans were prosperous beyond the dreams of the Europeans and Asians whose economies the war had destroyed.","locateZh":"美国和美国人富裕程度远超欧洲人和亚洲人的想象，而后者的经济已被战争摧毁。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文从未提及美国为获取领先地位付出 painstaking efforts；恰恰相反，首句强调的是 long and effortless success。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文 a market eight times larger than any competitor，比较对象是”任何对手”；选项偷改为 eight times larger than before（比”以前”大），且把”市场规模”当成原因本身，而非领先地位的表现之一。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"C 项把定位句 whose economies the war had destroyed 的因果完整重写，主语、宾语、谓语一一对应，且无任何添加，符合预判。","pairs":[{"orig":"the Europeans and Asians whose economies the war had destroyed","opt":"the war had destroyed the economies of most potential competitors"},{"orig":"the Europeans and Asians","opt":"most potential competitors"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文中 unparalleled 修饰的是 economies of scale（规模经济），而非 workforce 的规模；且原文称工人是 the most skilled（最熟练），未提其 size。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":12,"stem":"The loss of U.S. predominance in the world economy in the 1980s is manifested in the fact that the American____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"TV industry had withdrawn to its domestic market"},{"key":"B","text":"semiconductor industry had been taken over by foreign enterprises"},{"key":"C","text":"machine-tool industry had collapsed after suicidal actions"},{"key":"D","text":"auto industry had lost part of its domestic market"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"20世纪80年代美国在世界经济中主导地位的丧失表现在美国____这一事实上。","choicesZh":{"A":"电视产业退回到国内市场","B":"半导体产业被外国企业接管","C":"机床产业在自杀式行动后崩溃","D":"汽车产业失去了部分国内市场"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 is manifested in the fact that the American____ 要求选出原文中体现衰退的具体事实，是对原文某具体表述的细节核对。","parse":"题干 The loss of U.S. predominance in the world economy in the 1980s is manifested in the fact that the American____ 主干为 The loss is manifested in the fact；that 引导同位语从句补足 fact 内容，American 后接的名词由选项补全。注意 manifested in 意为”通过……体现”，不是”导致”。","locateEn":"Foreign-made cars and textiles were sweeping into the domestic market.","locateZh":"外国制造的汽车和纺织品正大举涌入美国国内市场。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文 By 1987 there was only one American television maker left, Zenith. (Now there is none: Zenith was bought by South Korea's LG Electronics in July.) 说的是只剩一家、且后来被韩国 LG 收购，根本谈不上”退守本土市场”。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文 For a while it looked as though the making of semiconductors...was going to be the next casualty. 是”一度看起来”会成为下一个牺牲品，是担忧/可能性，且文章并未说半导体业已被外企接管。选项把可能性当成事实。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文 America's machine-tool industry was on the ropes. 意为”陷入困境/濒临崩溃”，是被外部竞争挤压的结果；选项却说是 suicidal actions（自杀式举动）造成的崩溃，自加”自杀式举动”这一原因。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"D 项是原文”外车涌入本土市场”事实的视角反转表达，且只说 lost part of its domestic market（部分份额），与原文 sweeping into 的语义强度相符。","pairs":[{"orig":"Foreign-made cars and textiles were sweeping into the domestic market.","opt":"auto industry had lost part of its domestic market"},{"orig":"cars","opt":"auto industry"}]}}}}},{"n":13,"stem":"What can be inferred from the passage?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is human nature to shift between self-doubt and blind pride."},{"key":"B","text":"Intense competition may contribute to economic progress."},{"key":"C","text":"The revival of the economy depends on international cooperation."},{"key":"D","text":"A long history of success may pave the way for further development."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"推断题","stemZh":"从文中可以推断出什么?","choicesZh":{"A":"在自我怀疑和盲目自负之间摇摆是人的本性。","B":"激烈的竞争可能有助于经济进步。","C":"经济复苏依赖于国际合作。","D":"长期的成功历史可能为进一步发展铺平道路。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 What can be inferred from the passage? 字面给出 inferred，指向全篇推断。","parse":"题干 What can be inferred from the passage? 是简单一般疑问句，被动语态 can be inferred 强调推断主体不限；passage 指全文，提示范围在全篇而非某段。无陷阱。","locateEn":"How things have changed! In 1995 the United States can look back on five years of solid growth while Japan has been struggling.","locateZh":"情况发生了多么大的变化！1995 年，美国可以回顾连续五年的稳健增长，而日本却一直在苦苦挣扎。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文确有 crisis of confidence 与 Self-doubt has yielded to blind pride. 的情绪变化描述，但只针对”那一代美国人”，并未上升到”人性”。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"B 用 may contribute（可能促进）这一克制语气表达全文主线，既覆盖全文事实，又留出推断必要的余地——典型的”稳妥推断”型正确项。","pairs":[{"orig":"Americans had found themselves at a loss over their fading industrial competitiveness.","opt":"Intense competition may contribute to economic progress."},{"orig":"All of this caused a crisis of confidence.","opt":"may contribute to economic progress"},{"orig":"American industry has changed its structure, has gone on a diet, has learnt to be more quick-witted","opt":"contribute to economic progress"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"全文谈的是 international competition（外部竞争），并未提及任何 international cooperation（国际合作）；恰恰相反，美国复苏靠的是对内的产业自我改革。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"全文开篇即点出 A history of long and effortless success can be a dreadful handicap——长久顺风顺水可能反而是负担。选项把它说成”为进一步发展铺路”，与原文论断方向相反。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":14,"stem":"The author seems to believe the revival of the U.S. economy in the 1990s can be attributed to the____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"turning of the business cycle"},{"key":"B","text":"restructuring of industry"},{"key":"C","text":"improved business management"},{"key":"D","text":"success in education"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"作者似乎认为20世纪90年代美国经济的复苏可以归因于____。","choicesZh":{"A":"商业周期的转变","B":"产业结构调整","C":"企业管理的改善","D":"教育的成功"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 can be attributed to the____ 要求选出作者归结的原因，本质是细节核对作者旁白对原因的判断。","parse":"题干 The author seems to believe the revival of the U.S. economy in the 1990s can be attributed to the____ 主干 The author believes（that 省略）the revival can be attributed to ...；attributed to 意为”归因于”，注意 seems to 暗示作者并非斩钉截铁，但仍是作者立场。","locateEn":"Few Americans attribute this solely to such obvious causes as a devalued dollar or the turning of the business cycle.","locateZh":"很少有美国人会把这次复苏完全归因于美元贬值或商业周期翻转这类显而易见的原因。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"A 项是定位句里原词照搬的归因选项，作者通过 Few...solely 与 obvious causes 暗示自己认为这是真正成因之一，与题干 seems to believe 的弱断言语气吻合。","pairs":[{"orig":"the turning of the business cycle","opt":"turning of the business cycle"},{"orig":"Few Americans attribute this solely to such obvious causes","opt":"turning of the business cycle"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"American industry has changed its structure 出自 Richard Cavanagh之口，属直接引语；这是被采访者的归因，不是作者本人的归因。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"our businesses are improving their productivity 出自 Stephen Moore；a golden age of business management 出自 William Sahlman。这些”管理改善”评价都来自被引者，不是作者旁白。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"全文未出现 education 或与教育相关的任何陈述；第 1 段提到 scientists were the world's best; its workers the most skilled，但说的是战后状态，不是 1990 年代复苏的原因。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-2","kind":"reading","title":"Text 2","textNo":2,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 2","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-1","text":"Being a man has always been dangerous. There are about 105 males born for every 100 females, but this ratio drops to near balance at the age of maturity, and among 70-year-olds there are twice as many women as men. But the great universal of male mortality is being changed. Now, boy babies survive almost as well as girls do. This means that, for the first time, there will be an excess of boys in those crucial years when they are searching for a mate. More important, another chance for natural selection has been removed. Fifty years ago, the chance of a baby (particularly a boy baby) surviving depended on its weight. A kilogram too light or too heavy meant almost certain death. Today it makes almost no difference. Since much of the variation is due to genes, one more agent of evolution has gone."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-2","text":"There is another way to commit evolutionary suicide: stay alive, but have fewer children. Few people are as fertile as in the past. Except in some religious communities, very few women have 15 children. Nowadays the number of births, like the age of death, has become average. Most of us have roughly the same number of offspring. Again, differences between people and the opportunity for natural selection to take advantage of it have diminished. India shows what is happening. The country offers wealth for a few in the great cities and poverty for the remaining tribal peoples. The grand mediocrity of today—everyone being the same in survival and number of offspring—means that natural selection has lost 80% of its power in upper-middle-class India compared to the tribes."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-3","text":"For us, this means that evolution is over; the biological Utopia has arrived. Strangely, it has involved little physical change. No other species fills so many places in nature. But in the past 100,000 years—even the past 100 years—our lives have been transformed but our bodies have not. We did not evolve, because machines and society did it for us. Darwin had a phrase to describe those ignorant of evolution: they \"look at an organic being as a savage looks at a ship, as at something wholly beyond his comprehension.\" No doubt we will remember a 20th century way of life beyond comprehension for its ugliness. But however amazed our descendants may be at how far from Utopia we were, they will look just like us."}]},"questions":[{"n":15,"stem":"What used to be the danger in being a man according to the first paragraph?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A lack of mates."},{"key":"B","text":"A fierce competition."},{"key":"C","text":"A lower survival rate."},{"key":"D","text":"A defective gene."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据第一段，过去作为男性的危险是什么?","choicesZh":{"A":"缺少配偶。","B":"激烈的竞争。","C":"较低的存活率。","D":"有缺陷的基因。"},"analysis":{"type":"What used to be the danger in being a man 问的是\"过去那种危险具体是什么\"，是回原文找一个客观事实，不要求推理或概括。","parse":"What used to be the danger in being a man according to the first paragraph 是一个 What 引导的特殊疑问句，主干是 What used to be the danger，used to be 表示\"过去曾经是\"，暗含\"现在已不再如此\"的对比；according to the first paragraph 是状语，限定证据来源。无陷阱。","locateEn":"Being a man has always been dangerous. There are about 105 males born for every 100 females, but this ratio drops to near balance at the age of maturity, and among 70-year-olds there are twice as many women as men.","locateZh":"做个男人一直都很危险。每出生 100 个女婴大约对应 105 个男婴，但到成年时这个比例就降到接近 1:1，而到了 70 岁这一代，女性是男性的两倍。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"A lack of mates 利用了 there will be an excess of boys in those crucial years when they are searching for a mate，但原文说的是 \"将来\" 会男多女少（for the first time），是变化后的新情况，不是 What used to be the danger 问的过去的危险。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"A fierce competition 在 P1 找不到对应；原文只谈男婴出生率、男性死亡率、出生体重，没有任何\"竞争\"语义。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判出\"男性活下来概率更低\"，正好就是 A lower survival rate 的中文翻译；C 是定位句的客观抽象。","pairs":[{"orig":"among 70-year-olds there are twice as many women as men","opt":"A lower survival rate"},{"orig":"Now, boy babies survive almost as well as girls do","opt":"A lower survival rate"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"A defective gene 利用了 Since much of the variation is due to genes, one more agent of evolution has gone，但原文说的是\"出生体重的差异由基因决定\"，根本没说男性有缺陷基因——variation due to genes ≠ defective gene。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":16,"stem":"What does the example of India illustrate?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Wealthy people tend to have fewer children than poor people."},{"key":"B","text":"Natural selection hardly works among the rich and the poor."},{"key":"C","text":"The middle class population is 80% smaller than that of the tribes."},{"key":"D","text":"India is one of the countries with a very high birth rate."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"印度的例子说明了什么?","choicesZh":{"A":"富人往往比穷人生育的孩子少。","B":"自然选择在富人和穷人之间几乎不起作用。","C":"中产阶级人口比部落人口少80%。","D":"印度是出生率非常高的国家之一。"},"analysis":{"type":"What does the example of India illustrate 明确把 India 定性为\"例子\"，问的是它服务于哪个论点，符合例证目的题的典型句式。","parse":"What does the example of India illustrate 是 What 引导的特殊疑问句，主干 What does the example illustrate，of India 是后置定语限定 example。无陷阱。","locateEn":"The grand mediocrity of today—everyone being the same in survival and number of offspring—means that natural selection has lost 80% of its power in upper-middle-class India compared to the tribes.","locateZh":"今天的\"大同质化\"——每个人在存活和子女数量上都差不多——意味着，与部落人群相比，自然选择在印度中上阶层身上已经失去了 80% 的力量。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Wealthy people tend to have fewer children than poor people 哪怕属实，也是例子本身的细节，不是 India 例子\"illustrate\"的那个论点；而且原文也没正面说富人比穷人少生孩子，只说\"今天大家生育数趋同\"。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判出\"贫富两端自然选择都失效\"，正好是 Natural selection hardly works among the rich and the poor 的字面意思——B 是 India 例子真正要证明的论点。","pairs":[{"orig":"natural selection has lost 80% of its power in upper-middle-class India compared to the tribes","opt":"Natural selection hardly works among the rich and the poor"},{"orig":"Again, differences between people and the opportunity for natural selection to take advantage of it have diminished","opt":"Natural selection hardly works among the rich and the poor"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"The middle class population is 80% smaller than that of the tribes 利用了 natural selection has lost 80% of its power in upper-middle-class India compared to the tribes 里的 80%，但原文 80% 修饰的是 power（自然选择的力量），不是 population（人口）。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"India is one of the countries with a very high birth rate 在 P2 完全无对应；原文谈的是\"现代社会大家生得差不多\"，根本没说 India 出生率高。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":17,"stem":"The author argues that our bodies have stopped evolving because____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"life has been improved by technological advance"},{"key":"B","text":"the number of female babies has been declining"},{"key":"C","text":"our species has reached the highest stage of evolution"},{"key":"D","text":"the difference between wealth and poverty is disappearing"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"作者认为我们的身体已经停止进化,因为____。","choicesZh":{"A":"技术进步改善了生活","B":"女婴的数量一直在下降","C":"我们的物种已经达到了进化的最高阶段","D":"贫富差距正在消失"},"analysis":{"type":"The author argues that our bodies have stopped evolving because 形式上是补全句子，实质是问\"作者给出的原因是什么\"，是对原文一句具体表述的客观转述。","parse":"The author argues that our bodies have stopped evolving because____ 是一个待补全陈述句。主句 The author argues + that 宾语从句 our bodies have stopped evolving，stop doing 表\"停止做某事\"；because 引导原因状语从句，从句缺失，由四个选项补出。无陷阱。","locateEn":"But in the past 100,000 years—even the past 100 years—our lives have been transformed but our bodies have not. We did not evolve, because machines and society did it for us.","locateZh":"但在过去 10 万年——甚至过去 100 年——我们的生活方式已被彻底改变，可我们的身体却没变。我们没有进化，因为机器和社会已经替我们进化了。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判出\"机器与社会替进化做了事\"，正好就是 life has been improved by technological advance 的实质——technological advance 是机器和社会的总称，improved life 是它带来的结果。","pairs":[{"orig":"machines and society did it for us","opt":"life has been improved by technological advance"},{"orig":"our lives have been transformed but our bodies have not","opt":"life has been improved by technological advance"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"the number of female babies has been declining 与 P1 中 105 男婴比 100 女婴的事实方向相反——原文是\"男婴多于女婴\"，且只在出生比上提到，未说女婴在 declining；与 Q17 因果完全无关。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"our species has reached the highest stage of evolution 利用了 the biological Utopia has arrived，但 Utopia 在原文是带反讽口吻的措辞（紧接着作者就吐槽 our descendants may be at how far from Utopia we were）——原文从未说人类已是进化的最高阶段，且这也不是 Q17 问的\"原因\"。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"the difference between wealth and poverty is disappearing 利用了 The grand mediocrity of today 的语义，但作者说的是\"存活与子女数趋同\"，不是\"贫富差异在消失\"——而且 Q17 问的是\"身体停止进化\"的原因，不在贫富差异。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":18,"stem":"Which of the following would be the best title for the passage?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Sex Ratio Changes in Human Evolution."},{"key":"B","text":"Ways of Continuing Man's Evolution."},{"key":"C","text":"The Evolutionary Future of Nature."},{"key":"D","text":"Human Evolution Going Nowhere."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"以下哪项是这篇文章的最佳标题?","choicesZh":{"A":"人类进化中的性别比例变化。","B":"延续人类进化的方式。","C":"自然的进化前景。","D":"人类进化走向终结。"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following would be the best title for the passage 问的是全文最佳标题，必须覆盖全文，不能只对应某一段。","parse":"Which of the following would be the best title for the passage 是一个 Which 引导的特殊疑问句，would 是虚拟语气表\"在所给选项中应是\"，主干 Which would be the best title。无陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Sex Ratio Changes in Human Evolution 只触到 There are about 105 males born for every 100 females 这部分内容，P2 与 P3 完全装不进，作为全文标题严重以偏概全。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Ways of Continuing Man's Evolution 默认了进化可以\"继续\"并给出方法，但全文论断恰恰是 evolution is over——作者根本不主张\"如何继续\"。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"The Evolutionary Future of Nature 利用了 No other species fills so many places in nature 里的 nature 一词，但全文真正讨论的对象是 human/man，不是 nature 整体；标题主语偷换。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"D 项的 Human Evolution 覆盖全文话题，Going Nowhere 同时对接 P1、P2、P3 三段的论据走向，并保留作者的微讽口吻——是唯一全覆盖且口吻一致的标题。","pairs":[{"orig":"evolution is over","opt":"Human Evolution Going Nowhere"},{"orig":"natural selection has lost 80% of its power","opt":"Human Evolution Going Nowhere"},{"orig":"another chance for natural selection has been removed","opt":"Human Evolution Going Nowhere"}]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-3","kind":"reading","title":"Text 3","textNo":3,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 3","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-1","text":"When a new movement in art attains a certain fashion, it is advisable to find out what its advocates are aiming at, for, however farfetched and unreasonable their principles may seem today, it is possible that in years to come they may be regarded as normal. With regard to Futurist poetry, however, the case is rather difficult, for whatever Futurist poetry may be—even admitting that the theory on which it is based may be right—it can hardly be classed as Literature."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-2","text":"This, in brief, is what the Futurist says: for a century, past conditions of life have been conditionally speeding up, till now we live in a world of noise and violence and speed. Consequently, our feelings, thoughts and emotions have undergone a corresponding change. This speeding up of life, says the Futurist, requires a new form of expression. We must speed up our literature too, if we want to interpret modern stress. We must pour out a large stream of essential words, unhampered by stops, or qualifying adjectives, or finite verbs. Instead of describing sounds we must make up words that imitate them; we must use many sizes of type and different colored inks on the same page, and shorten or lengthen words at will."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-3","text":"Certainly their descriptions of battles are confused. But it is a little upsetting to read in the explanatory notes that a certain line describes a fight between a Turkish and a Bulgarian officer on a bridge off which they both fall into the river—and then to find that the line consists of the noise of their falling and the weights of the officers: \"Pluff! Pluff! A hundred and eighty-five kilograms.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-4","text":"This, though it fulfills the laws and requirements of Futurist poetry, can hardly be classed as Literature. All the same, no thinking man can refuse to accept their first proposition: that a great change in our emotional life calls for a change of expression. The whole question is really this: have we essentially changed?"}]},"questions":[{"n":19,"stem":"This passage is mainly____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"a survey of new approaches to art"},{"key":"B","text":"a review of Futurist poetry"},{"key":"C","text":"about merits of the Futurist movement"},{"key":"D","text":"about laws and requirements of literature"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"这篇文章主要是____。","choicesZh":{"A":"对艺术新方法的调查","B":"对未来主义诗歌的评论","C":"关于未来主义运动的优点","D":"关于文学的规律和要求"},"analysis":{"type":"This passage is mainly 同时具备主旨标记 mainly 与范围词 passage，是教科书式的主旨题题干。","parse":"This passage is mainly____. 是主系表残缺结构，空格紧跟系动词 is 后的状语 mainly，四个选项都是名词性短语充当表语，结构平铺直叙、无陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"全文只评 Futurist poetry 这一种新艺术运动，并非泛泛 a survey of new approaches to art，从未横向比较其他艺术新方法。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"a review of Futurist poetry 既圈定了正确对象，也以 review 涵盖了全文\"陈述主张 + 例证审视 + 评价收束\"的复合动作，与预判完全一致。","pairs":[{"orig":"With regard to Futurist poetry","opt":"a review of Futurist poetry"},{"orig":"can hardly be classed as Literature","opt":"a review of Futurist poetry"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"全文对 Futurist 诗歌持否定态度（it can hardly be classed as Literature、can hardly be classed as Literature），不可能是 about merits of the Futurist movement\"谈未来主义运动的优点\"，方向相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文 fulfills the laws and requirements of Futurist poetry 谈的是 Futurist 诗歌内部规则，不是 laws and requirements of literature\"文学一般规则\"；全文也未系统阐述文学规则。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":20,"stem":"When a novel literary idea appears, people should try to____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"determine its purposes"},{"key":"B","text":"ignore its flaws"},{"key":"C","text":"follow the new fashions"},{"key":"D","text":"accept the principles"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"当一种新颖的文学观念出现时,人们应该试图____。","choicesZh":{"A":"确定其目的","B":"忽视其缺陷","C":"追随新潮流","D":"接受其原则"},"analysis":{"type":"people should try to 要求填一个具体动作，是对原文某句客观陈述的复述，不需要推断，属于典型细节题。","parse":"When a novel literary idea appears, people should try to____. 是 when 时间状语从句 + 主句结构，主句的不定式宾语被截断为空格，四个选项分别补出宾语动词原形，结构直白。","locateEn":"When a new movement in art attains a certain fashion, it is advisable to find out what its advocates are aiming at, for, however farfetched and unreasonable their principles may seem today, it is possible that in years to come they may be regarded as normal.","locateZh":"当一种新的艺术运动开始流行时，弄清其倡导者意图所在是明智之举，因为无论他们的主张在今天看起来多么牵强、不合理，多年以后这些主张都有可能被视为寻常。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判答案是\"弄清倡导者的目的\"，determine its purposes 直接对应这一语义，是定位句的同义替换。","pairs":[{"orig":"find out what its advocates are aiming at","opt":"determine its purposes"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说要弄清主张是什么，并没有让人 ignore its flaws（忽视其缺陷），属凭空增添的动作。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文要求 find out what its advocates are aiming at 是认知层面的弄清，而 follow the new fashions 是行为层面的追随，二者语义不同。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文只让人 find out（弄清）主张，并未要求 accept the principles（接受主张），且作者随后明确否定 Futurist 主张可归为文学，更不可能要人无条件接受。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":21,"stem":"Futurists claim that we must____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"increase the production of literature"},{"key":"B","text":"use poetry to relieve modern stress"},{"key":"C","text":"develop new modes of expression"},{"key":"D","text":"avoid using adjectives and verbs"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"未来主义者声称我们必须____。","choicesZh":{"A":"增加文学作品的产量","B":"用诗歌来缓解现代压力","C":"发展新的表达方式","D":"避免使用形容词和动词"},"analysis":{"type":"Futurists claim that we must____. 问的是 Futurists 明确提出的具体主张，属对原文陈述的客观转述。","parse":"Futurists claim that we must____. 是主句 + that 宾语从句，从句主语 we 后接情态动词 must，空格处补出 must 之后的动词原形短语；结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"We must speed up our literature too, if we want to interpret modern stress. We must pour out a large stream of essential words, unhampered by stops, or qualifying adjectives, or finite verbs. Instead of describing sounds we must make up words that imitate them; we must use many sizes of type and different colored inks on the same page, and shorten or lengthen words at will.","locateZh":"如果想表达现代张力，我们也必须给文学提速。我们必须倾泻出大量本质性的词语，不被句号、修饰性形容词或限定动词所拖累。我们不能描述声音，而要造出模拟声音的词；必须在同一页上使用多种字号和不同颜色的墨水，还要随心所欲地拉长或缩短单词。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文 We must speed up our literature too 是\"加快文学（节奏）\"，并非 increase the production of literature\"增加文学产量\"，二者完全不同。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文是 if we want to interpret modern stress——\"为了表达现代张力\"才要改造文学，而 use poetry to relieve modern stress 却说\"用诗歌来缓解现代张力\"，把\"表达\"换成\"缓解\"，方向相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判答案是\"为文学发明新的表达形式\"，develop new modes of expression 直接对应 requires a new form of expression，且能覆盖第二段所有 we must 句的公约数。","pairs":[{"orig":"We must speed up our literature too, if we want to interpret modern stress","opt":"develop new modes of expression"},{"orig":"This speeding up of life, says the Futurist, requires a new form of expression","opt":"develop new modes of expression"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文 unhampered by stops, or qualifying adjectives, or finite verbs 说的是新文学不被句号、修饰形容词、限定动词\"拖累\"，并非全面 avoid using adjectives and verbs——既漏掉了 stops，又把\"qualifying adjectives / finite verbs\"扩大成所有 adjectives and verbs。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":22,"stem":"The author believes that Futurist poetry is____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"based on reasonable principles"},{"key":"B","text":"new and acceptable to ordinary people"},{"key":"C","text":"indicative of a basic change in human nature"},{"key":"D","text":"more of a transient phenomenon than literature"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"态度题","stemZh":"作者认为未来主义诗歌是____。","choicesZh":{"A":"基于合理的原则","B":"新颖且为普通人所接受","C":"表明人性发生了根本变化","D":"与其说是文学不如说是一种短暂现象"},"analysis":{"type":"The author believes that Futurist poetry is____ 直接问\"作者认为 X 是怎样的\"，是标准的作者态度题。","parse":"The author believes that Futurist poetry is____. 是主句 + that 宾语从句，从句\"Futurist poetry is + 表语\"，空格即表语；语法简单，注意四个选项都是评价性短语，要靠态度词极性区分。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文 however farfetched and unreasonable their principles may seem today 反而把其原则贴上\"牵强不合理\"的标签，与 based on reasonable principles 直接相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文从未讨论 Futurist 诗歌是否 new and acceptable to ordinary people\"为普通人所接受\"——这是凭空增添的评价维度。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文 have we essentially changed? 明白把\"人是否本质改变\"作为未决之问；C 项却让作者断言 Futurist 诗歌 indicative of a basic change in human nature，把疑问句直接当结论。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"more of a transient phenomenon than literature 同时命中\"不算真正的文学\"与\"短期/过渡\"两层语义，与全文负面+悬置的总评极性高度吻合。","pairs":[{"orig":"it can hardly be classed as Literature","opt":"more of a transient phenomenon than literature"},{"orig":"have we essentially changed?","opt":"more of a transient phenomenon than literature"}]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-4","kind":"reading","title":"Text 4","textNo":4,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 4","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-1","text":"Aimlessness has hardly been typical of the postwar Japan whose productivity and social harmony are the envy of the United States and Europe. But increasingly the Japanese are seeing a decline of the traditional work-moral values. Ten years ago young people were hardworking and saw their jobs as their primary reason for being, but now Japan has largely fulfilled its economic needs, and young people don't know where they should go next."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-2","text":"The coming of age of the postwar baby boom and an entry of women into the male-dominated job market have limited the opportunities of teenagers who are already questioning the heavy personal sacrifices involved in climbing Japan's rigid social ladder to good schools and jobs. In a recent survey, it was found that only 24.5 percent of Japanese students were fully satisfied with school life, compared with 67.2 percent of students in the United States. In addition, far more Japanese workers expressed dissatisfaction with their jobs than did their counterparts in the 10 other countries surveyed."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-3","text":"While often praised by foreigners for its emphasis on the basics, Japanese education tends to stress test taking and mechanical learning over creativity and self-expression. \"Those things that do not show up in the test scores—personality, ability, courage or humanity—are completely ignored,\" says Toshiki Kaifu, chairman of the ruling Liberal Democratic Party's education committee. \"Frustration against this kind of thing leads kids to drop out and run wild.\" Last year Japan experienced 2,125 incidents of school violence, including 929 assaults on teachers. Amid the outcry, many conservative leaders are seeking a return to the prewar emphasis on moral education. Last year Mitsuo Setoyama, who was then education minister, raised eyebrows when he argued that liberal reforms introduced by the American occupation authorities after World War II had weakened the \"Japanese morality of respect for parents.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-4","text":"But that may have more to do with Japanese life-styles. \"In Japan,\" says educator Yoko Muro, \"it's never a question of whether you enjoy your job and your life, but only how much you can endure.\" With economic growth has come centralization; fully 76 percent of Japan's 119 million citizens live in cities where community and the extended family have been abandoned in favor of isolated, two-generation households. Urban Japanese have long endured lengthy commutes (travels to and from work) and crowded living conditions, but as the old group and family values weaken, the discomfort is beginning to tell. In the past decade, the Japanese divorce rate, while still well below that of the United States, has increased by more than 50 percent, and suicides have increased by nearly one-quarter."}]},"questions":[{"n":23,"stem":"In the Westerners' eyes, the postwar Japan was____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"under aimless development"},{"key":"B","text":"a positive example"},{"key":"C","text":"a rival to the West"},{"key":"D","text":"on the decline"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"在西方人眼中,战后的日本____。","choicesZh":{"A":"处于漫无目的的发展之中","B":"一个正面的榜样","C":"西方的竞争对手","D":"正在衰落"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 In the Westerners' eyes, the postwar Japan was____ 是对客观事实（西方人如何看待战后日本）的判断，未出现 infer/suggest/imply 等推理动词。","parse":"句子主干为 the postwar Japan was____，前置状语 In the Westerners' eyes 表视角；考生需理解 the postwar Japan 是被评价对象、Westerners 是评价主体，二者一旦对调即整句失真。","locateEn":"Aimlessness has hardly been typical of the postwar Japan whose productivity and social harmony are the envy of the United States and Europe.","locateZh":"漫无目的从来不是战后日本的特征——战后日本的生产率与社会和谐令美国和欧洲艳羡。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"under aimless development 即\"漫无目的地发展\"，而原文明确说 Aimlessness has hardly been typical of the postwar Japan，A 项与原文极性相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判\"令西方艳羡的正面对象\"与 a positive example 完全同义；其余选项均与定位句极性或对象不符。","pairs":[{"orig":"the envy of the United States and Europe","opt":"a positive example"},{"orig":"Aimlessness has hardly been typical of the postwar Japan","opt":"a positive example"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"a rival to the West（西方的对手）暗含敌对/竞争关系，原文只说西方对日本生产率与社会和谐\"艳羡\"，未提任何对抗或竞争关系。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"on the decline 指\"在走下坡路\"，而原文说战后日本生产率与社会和谐 the envy of the United States and Europe，是上升/榜样状态；本段后文谈\"工作道德下滑\"是另一话题，不能套到\"西方人眼中的战后日本\"上。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":24,"stem":"According to the author, what may chiefly be responsible for the moral decline of Japanese society?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Women's participation in social activities is limited."},{"key":"B","text":"More workers are dissatisfied with their jobs."},{"key":"C","text":"Excessive emphasis has been placed on the basics."},{"key":"D","text":"The life-style has been influenced by Western values."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据作者的观点,什么可能是日本社会道德衰退的主要原因?","choicesZh":{"A":"女性参与社会活动受到限制。","B":"更多的工人对自己的工作不满意。","C":"过分强调了基础知识。","D":"生活方式受到了西方价值观的影响。"},"analysis":{"type":"According to the author, what may chiefly be responsible for 要求按作者明示的归因作答，原文有显式因果句，不需考生跨段推理。","parse":"情态动词 may 与 chiefly 共同限定 be responsible for：may 留出措辞余地、chiefly 排除次要原因；考生若漏看 chiefly，会被原文里的次要原因（如教育、工作不满）干扰。","locateEn":"But that may have more to do with Japanese life-styles. \"In Japan,\" says educator Yoko Muro, \"it's never a question of whether you enjoy your job and your life, but only how much you can endure.\" With economic growth has come centralization; fully 76 percent of Japan's 119 million citizens live in cities where community and the extended family have been abandoned in favor of isolated, two-generation households.","locateZh":"但那也许更多与日本的生活方式有关。教育家 Yoko Muro 说：\"在日本，从不问你是否享受工作和生活，只问你能忍多久。\"伴随经济增长而来的是中心化：日本 1.19 亿人口中 76% 居住在城市，传统社区与大家庭被舍弃，让位于孤立的两代家庭。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Women's participation in social activities is limited. 与原文 an entry of women into the male-dominated job market 极性相反——原文说女性正在进入职场，而非受限。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"More workers are dissatisfied with their jobs. 对应 far more Japanese workers expressed dissatisfaction with their jobs，原文有此事实，但它只是道德下滑的表现/伴随现象，不是作者明示的\"主因\"——主因明示在第 4 段 that may have more to do with Japanese life-styles。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Excessive emphasis has been placed on the basics. 把 often praised by foreigners for its emphasis on the basics 的\"外国人对基础教育的赞赏\"偷换成\"过度强调基础\"；原文用 often praised 是肯定语气，并未说 excessive，且这是教育层面而非道德下滑主因。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判主因为\"日本生活方式\"；而原文上一段 liberal reforms introduced by the American occupation authorities 已交代该生活方式来源——美国占领后的自由改革，The life-style has been influenced by Western values 正是这一链条的整合表述。","pairs":[{"orig":"With economic growth has come centralization; fully 76 percent of Japan's 119 million citizens live in cities where community and the extended family have been abandoned in favor of isolated, two-generation households","opt":"The life-style has been influenced by Western values."},{"orig":"But that may have more to do with Japanese life-styles","opt":"The life-style has been influenced by Western values."}]}}}}},{"n":25,"stem":"Which of the following is true according to the author____?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Japanese education is praised for helping the young climb the social ladder."},{"key":"B","text":"Japanese education is characterized by mechanical learning as well as creativity."},{"key":"C","text":"More stress should be placed on the cultivation of creativity."},{"key":"D","text":"Dropping out leads to frustration against test taking."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据作者的观点,下列哪一项是正确的____?","choicesZh":{"A":"日本教育因帮助年轻人攀登社会阶梯而受到赞扬。","B":"日本教育的特点是机械学习和创造力并重。","C":"应该更加重视创造力的培养。","D":"辍学导致对应试的挫败感。"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following is true according to the author 四个选项均是关于日本教育的事实陈述，正确项与原文存在直接同义替换关系，无需跨段推理。","parse":"题干为不完整疑问 Which of the following is true according to the author____，下划线只是版式残留；考生若误读为\"作者认为以下哪项不正确\"会全题反向；according to the author 是限定状语，过滤掉 Kaifu 等他人引语。","locateEn":"While often praised by foreigners for its emphasis on the basics, Japanese education tends to stress test taking and mechanical learning over creativity and self-expression.","locateZh":"尽管常因重视基础而被外国人赞赏，日本教育却倾向于把应试与机械学习置于创造力与自我表达之上。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Japanese education is praised for helping the young climb the social ladder. 原文 often praised by foreigners for its emphasis on the basics 中赞赏的内容是\"重视基础\"，并非\"帮助年轻人攀登社会阶梯\"；社会阶梯一词出现在 climbing Japan's rigid social ladder，是青少年付出的代价而非教育被赞之处，两处被强行拼接。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Japanese education is characterized by mechanical learning as well as creativity. 把 mechanical learning 与 creativity 并列；原文明确二者对立——stress test taking and mechanical learning over creativity and self-expression 与 personality, ability, courage or humanity—are completely ignored。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判\"作者主张抬高创造力培养\"与 More stress should be placed on the cultivation of creativity 完全同义；其他三项均与作者立场或原文事实冲突。","pairs":[{"orig":"Japanese education tends to stress test taking and mechanical learning over creativity and self-expression","opt":"More stress should be placed on the cultivation of creativity."},{"orig":"\"Those things that do not show up in the test scores—personality, ability, courage or humanity—are completely ignored,\"","opt":"More stress should be placed on the cultivation of creativity."}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Dropping out leads to frustration against test taking. 把原文 Frustration against this kind of thing leads kids to drop out and run wild. 的因果颠倒——原文是\"对应试压抑的挫败 → 辍学\"，选项倒成\"辍学 → 对应试的挫败\"。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":26,"stem":"The change in Japanese life-style is revealed in the fact that____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the young are less tolerant of discomforts in life"},{"key":"B","text":"the divorce rate in Japan exceeds that in the U.S."},{"key":"C","text":"the Japanese endure more than ever before"},{"key":"D","text":"the Japanese appreciate their present life"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"日本生活方式的变化体现在____这一事实上。","choicesZh":{"A":"年轻人对生活中的不适越来越不能容忍","B":"日本的离婚率超过了美国","C":"日本人比以往任何时候都更能忍耐","D":"日本人珍惜他们现在的生活"},"analysis":{"type":"The change in Japanese life-style is revealed in the fact that____ 要求选出原文已陈述的事实，四个选项均为可证伪的客观陈述，无推理动词。","parse":"句子主干 The change...is revealed in the fact that____，that 引导同位语从句承载\"事实内容\"；考生若把 reveal（揭示）误解成\"导致\"或\"掩盖\"会全题失真。","locateEn":"In the past decade, the Japanese divorce rate, while still well below that of the United States, has increased by more than 50 percent, and suicides have increased by nearly one-quarter.","locateZh":"在过去十年里，日本的离婚率虽仍远低于美国，但已上升 50% 以上，自杀率也上升了近四分之一。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判\"对不适忍耐力下降\"与 the young are less tolerant of discomforts in life 完全同义；其余选项均与原文事实或方向冲突。","pairs":[{"orig":"as the old group and family values weaken, the discomfort is beginning to tell","opt":"the young are less tolerant of discomforts in life"},{"orig":"the Japanese divorce rate, while still well below that of the United States, has increased by more than 50 percent, and suicides have increased by nearly one-quarter","opt":"the young are less tolerant of discomforts in life"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"the divorce rate in Japan exceeds that in the U.S.（日本离婚率超过美国）与原文 still well below that of the United States 直接相反——原文明示日本离婚率仍\"远低于\"美国。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"the Japanese endure more than ever before（日本人比以前更能忍）与原文 the discomfort is beginning to tell 与 Muro 引语 only how much you can endure 的语境相反——原文要点是\"忍受到达临界、开始忍不下去\"，并非更能忍。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"the Japanese appreciate their present life（欣赏当下生活）与全段基调相反——原文用 lengthy commutes、crowded living conditions、divorce rate...increased by more than 50 percent、suicides have increased 渲染负面状态。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-5","kind":"reading","title":"Text 5","textNo":5,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 5","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-5-1","text":"If ambition is to be well regarded, the rewards of ambition—wealth, distinction, control over one's destiny—must be deemed worthy of the sacrifices made on ambition's behalf. If the tradition of ambition is to have vitality, it must be widely shared; and it especially must be highly regarded by people who are themselves admired, the educated not least among them. In an odd way, however, it is the educated who have claimed to have given up on ambition as an ideal. What is odd is that they have perhaps most benefited from ambition—if not always their own then that of their parents and grandparents. There is a heavy note of hypocrisy in this, a case of closing the barn door after the horses have escaped—with the educated themselves riding on them."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-5-2","text":"Certainly people do not seem less interested in success and its signs now than formerly. Summer homes, European travel, BMWs—the locations, place names and name brands may change, but such items do not seem less in demand today than a decade or two years ago. What has happened is that people cannot confess fully to their dreams, as easily and openly as once they could, lest they be thought pushing, acquisitive and vulgar. Instead, we are treated to fine hypocritical spectacles, which now more than ever seem in ample supply: the critic of American materialism with a Southampton summer home; the publisher of radical books who takes his meals in three-star restaurants; the journalist advocating participatory democracy in all phases of life, whose own children are enrolled in private schools. For such people and many more perhaps not so exceptional, the proper formulation is, \"Succeed at all costs but avoid appearing ambitious.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-5-3","text":"The attacks on ambition are many and come from various angles; its public defenders are few and unimpressive, where they are not extremely unattractive. As a result, the support for ambition as a healthy impulse, a quality to be admired and fixed in the mind of the young, is probably lower than it has ever been in the United States. This does not mean that ambition is at an end, that people no longer feel its stirrings and promptings, but only that, no longer openly honored, it is less openly professed. Consequences follow from this, of course, some of which are that ambition is driven underground, or made sly. Such, then, is the way things stand: on the left angry critics, on the right stupid supporters, and in the middle, as usual, the majority of earnest people trying to get on in life."}]},"questions":[{"n":27,"stem":"It is generally believed that ambition may be well regarded if____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"its returns well compensate for the sacrifices"},{"key":"B","text":"it is rewarded with money, fame and power"},{"key":"C","text":"its goals are spiritual rather than material"},{"key":"D","text":"it is shared by the rich and the famous"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"人们普遍认为，如果____，雄心壮志可能会受到好评。","choicesZh":{"A":"它的回报足以补偿所做的牺牲","B":"它能获得金钱、名誉和权力的回报","C":"它的目标是精神层面的而非物质层面的","D":"它为富人和名人所共有"},"analysis":{"type":"It is generally believed that ambition may be well regarded if____. 是补全句，要求从原文找出 \"ambition 被认可\" 所附带的条件，无 infer/imply 等推断信号。","parse":"It is generally believed that ambition may be well regarded if____. 是 \"It is believed that+主句+if 条件状语从句\" 结构，重心在 if 之后——补全的是 ambition 被认可所需的条件，无陷阱。","locateEn":"If ambition is to be well regarded, the rewards of ambition—wealth, distinction, control over one's destiny—must be deemed worthy of the sacrifices made on ambition's behalf.","locateZh":"若雄心要被人们认可，其回报——财富、声望、对自身命运的掌控——就必须被视为值得为雄心所付出的牺牲。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"its returns well compensate for the sacrifices 把定位句拆出的 \"回报抵得上牺牲\" 改成主动句，与预判完全吻合。","pairs":[{"orig":"the rewards of ambition—wealth, distinction, control over one's destiny—must be deemed worthy of the sacrifices made on ambition's behalf","opt":"its returns well compensate for the sacrifices"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"it is rewarded with money, fame and power 只复述了原文 wealth, distinction, control over one's destiny 的列举，丢掉了原文最关键的条件 \"deemed worthy of the sacrifices\"——条件不见了，命题就不成立。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文列出的回报 wealth, distinction, control over one's destiny 全是物质或世俗目标；its goals are spiritual rather than material 把回报说成 \"精神而非物质\"，正好与原文相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"it is shared by the rich and the famous 谈的是\"被谁分享\"，与题干所问 \"何时被认可\" 的条件无关；原文谈的是 \"广泛分享 + 受 educated 推崇\"（it must be widely shared; and it especially must be highly regarded by people who are themselves admired, the educated not least among them.），并非 \"the rich and the famous\"。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":28,"stem":"The last sentence of the first paragraph most probably implies that it is____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"customary of the educated to discard ambition in words"},{"key":"B","text":"too late to check ambition once it has been let out"},{"key":"C","text":"dishonest to deny ambition after the fulfillment of the goal"},{"key":"D","text":"impractical for the educated to enjoy benefits from ambition"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"推断题","stemZh":"第一段的最后一句话很可能暗示____。","choicesZh":{"A":"受过教育的人习惯于在言辞上摒弃雄心壮志","B":"雄心壮志一旦释放出来就为时已晚无法遏制","C":"在目标实现后否认雄心壮志是不诚实的","D":"受过教育的人享受雄心壮志带来的好处是不切实际的"},"analysis":{"type":"most probably implies 是典型推断题信号词，问的是字面之外的言外之意。","parse":"The last sentence of the first paragraph most probably implies that it is____. 是 \"主语+谓语 implies+that 宾语从句\"，宾从内容由补全部分承担；it 是宾从形式主语，待补全的是表语，结构清晰。","locateEn":"There is a heavy note of hypocrisy in this, a case of closing the barn door after the horses have escaped—with the educated themselves riding on them.","locateZh":"这其中带着浓重的伪善味——好比马已跑出后才去关谷仓门，而受教育者本人正骑在那些马上。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"customary of the educated to discard ambition in words 只说\"惯于口头放弃\"，把原文里最关键的 heavy note of hypocrisy 的伪善评价丢了——隐喻句的精髓是\"事后\"和\"伪善\"，而非\"惯常\"。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"too late to check ambition once it has been let out 只翻译了 closing the barn door after the horses have escaped 的字面（为时已晚），把作者真正要类比的本体——\"受教育者已享受成果再否认 ambition\"——完全丢掉了；况且原文也不是说要 check（约束）ambition。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原句要点有二——hypocrisy（伪善/不诚实）+ already benefited（已经享受）；dishonest to deny ambition after the fulfillment of the goal 两点全中。","pairs":[{"orig":"a heavy note of hypocrisy in this, a case of closing the barn door after the horses have escaped—with the educated themselves riding on them","opt":"dishonest to deny ambition after the fulfillment of the goal"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文恰恰说 they have perhaps most benefited from ambition——受教育者最受益于 ambition；impractical for the educated to enjoy benefits from ambition 反过来说 \"受教育者享受 ambition 的好处不切实际\"，与原文相反。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":29,"stem":"Some people do not openly admit they have ambition because____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"they think of it as immoral"},{"key":"B","text":"their pursuits are not fame or wealth"},{"key":"C","text":"ambition is not closely related to material benefits"},{"key":"D","text":"they do not want to appear greedy and contemptible"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"有些人不公开承认自己有雄心壮志，因为____。","choicesZh":{"A":"他们认为这是不道德的","B":"他们追求的不是名声或财富","C":"雄心壮志与物质利益关系不大","D":"他们不想显得贪婪和卑鄙"},"analysis":{"type":"Some people do not openly admit they have ambition because____. 是 because 引导的原因补全句，要求从原文找到导致该现象的具体原因。","parse":"Some people do not openly admit they have ambition because____. 主句+because 原因从句结构；要补全的是原因，主句已陈述事实，须从原文找匹配的因果句。","locateEn":"What has happened is that people cannot confess fully to their dreams, as easily and openly as once they could, lest they be thought pushing, acquisitive and vulgar.","locateZh":"实际发生的是：人们再也不能像从前那样轻松、公开地坦白自己的梦想，唯恐被视作好出风头、贪得无厌、庸俗不堪。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"they think of it as immoral 把原文\"怕被人看成贪婪庸俗\"（社交评价/面子）拔高到 \"自己认为它不道德\"（道德判断）；原文从未说人们自己道德上否定 ambition，只说怕被外界这样看待。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文整段强调人们 do not seem less interested in success and its signs——对成功的标志（避暑别墅、欧洲游、BMW）兴趣未减；their pursuits are not fame or wealth 反过来说他们追求的不是名利，与原文相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"ambition is not closely related to material benefits 谈的是 ambition 与物质回报的关系，跟题干所问的 \"为什么不公开承认\" 无关；且原文一直把 ambition 和 wealth/Summer homes/BMW 紧密绑定，反向也站不住。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"they do not want to appear greedy and contemptible 既对上了原文 \"lest…be thought\" 的动机结构，又对上了 acquisitive/vulgar 的形容词语义场。","pairs":[{"orig":"lest they be thought pushing, acquisitive and vulgar","opt":"they do not want to appear greedy and contemptible"}]}}}}},{"n":30,"stem":"From the last paragraph the conclusion can be drawn that ambition should be maintained____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"secretly and vigorously"},{"key":"B","text":"openly and enthusiastically"},{"key":"C","text":"easily and momentarily"},{"key":"D","text":"verbally and spiritually"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"推断题","stemZh":"从最后一段可以得出结论，雄心壮志应该____地保持。","choicesZh":{"A":"秘密而有力","B":"公开而热情","C":"轻松而短暂","D":"口头上和精神上"},"analysis":{"type":"the conclusion can be drawn 显示本题不是直接细节，而是要从末段事实推出作者的隐含主张。","parse":"From the last paragraph the conclusion can be drawn that ambition should be maintained____. 是 \"From+地点状语+主句+that 同位语从句\" 结构；待补全的是 maintained 之后的方式状语（副词），暗示选项是 \"副词+副词\" 组合。","locateEn":"This does not mean that ambition is at an end, that people no longer feel its stirrings and promptings, but only that, no longer openly honored, it is less openly professed. Consequences follow from this, of course, some of which are that ambition is driven underground, or made sly.","locateZh":"这并不意味着 ambition 已走到尽头、人们不再感到它的冲动与召唤，只是说：它不再被公开尊崇，也就更少被公开表白。由此带来一些后果——比如 ambition 被驱入地下，或变得阴鸷狡黠。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"secretly and vigorously 里的 secretly 恰好是作者所批评的 driven underground, or made sly 的同义近义——作者反对地下化，干扰项却让人们继续 secretly，正好与作者立场相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"openly and enthusiastically 一头复现作者赞许的 openly，一头取反作者批评的 underground/sly，正反两面同时贴合，是末段立场的完整还原。","pairs":[{"orig":"no longer openly honored, it is less openly professed","opt":"openly and enthusiastically"},{"orig":"ambition is driven underground, or made sly","opt":"openly and enthusiastically"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"easily and momentarily 中的 momentarily（一瞬间地、短暂地）在末段完全无对应，作者主张的是长期持续地维护 ambition，而非 \"短暂地\"；easily 也偏\"轻松/随便\"，与作者所呼吁的\"公开、堂堂正正\"调性不符。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"verbally and spiritually 把作者主张的 \"openly（公开地、明面上）\" 偷换成 \"verbally（口头上）\"——但作者全文恰恰在批判 Succeed at all costs but avoid appearing ambitious 这种\"只在口头否认 ambition\"的伪善，所以\"仅口头维护\"也不是作者的立场；spiritually（精神上）原文亦无对应。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-b","kind":"translation","title":"Section II Part C 英译汉","directions":"Directions: Read the following text carefully and then translate the underlined segments into Chinese. Write your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. ( 10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-b-1","text":"Governments throughout the world act on the assumption that the welfare of their people depends largely on the economic strength and wealth of the community. (31) Under modern conditions, this requires varying measures of centralized control and hence the help of specialized scientists such as economists and operational research experts. (32) Furthermore, it is obvious that the strength of a country's economy is directly bound up with the efficiency of its agriculture and industry, and that this in turn rests upon the efforts of scientists and technologists of all kinds. It also means that governments are increasingly compelled to interfere in these sectors in order to step up production and ensure that it is utilized to the best advantage. For example, they may encourage research in various ways, including the setting up of their own research centers; they may alter the structure of education, or interfere in order to reduce the wastage of natural resources or tap resources hitherto unexploited; or they may cooperate directly in the growing number of international projects related to science, economics and industry. In any case, all such interventions are heavily dependent on scientific advice and also scientific and technological manpower of all kinds."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-2","text":"(33) Owing to the remarkable development in mass-communications, people everywhere are feeling new wants and are being exposed to new customs and ideas, while governments are often forced to introduce still further innovations for the reasons given above. At the same time, the normal rate of social change throughout the world is taking place at a vastly accelerated speed compared with the past. For example, (34) in the early industrialized countries of Europe the process of industrialization—with all the far-reaching changes in social patterns that followed—was spread over nearly a century, whereas nowadays a developing nation may undergo the same process in a decade or so. All this has the effect of building up unusual pressures and tensions within the community and consequently presents serious problems for the governments concerned. (35) Additional social stresses may also occur because of the population explosion or problems arising from mass migration movements—themselves made relatively easy nowadays by modern means of transport. As a result of all these factors, governments are becoming increasingly dependent on biologists and social scientists for planning the appropriate programs and putting them into effect."}]},"sentences":[{"n":31,"en":"Under modern conditions, this requires varying measures of centralized control and hence the help of specialized scientists such as economists and operational research experts.","refZh":"在现代条件下，这一点要求采取程度不一的集中管控措施，因而也需要诸如经济学家、运筹学专家这样的专业科学家提供帮助。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Under modern conditions,","lit":"在现代条件下，","role":"（条件状语）","note":"难点： modern conditions 不要漏译 Under modern conditions 是句首状语，看似简单但是采分点之一。译为「在现代条件下」最稳，不要润色成「如今」而把 modern 的「现代」内涵削弱。"},{"en":"this requires varying measures of centralized control","lit":"这就需要程度不一的集中管控措施","role":"（主干主谓宾）","note":"难点： this 回指 + varying 译「不同程度的」 this 回指上一句「民生依赖经济实力」这一前提；可译「这一点」或「要做到这一点」。varying measures 不是「变化的措施」，varying 在此是「不同程度／各种各样的」之意，译「程度不一的／各种各样的集中管控措施」。centralized control 直译「集中管控／集中控制」。"},{"en":"and hence the help of specialized scientists","lit":"因而也需要专业科学家的帮助","role":"（并列宾语 + 因果连接词）","note":"难点： hence = 因而／从而 hence 是结果连词，承前 requires，等价于「因此也需要…」。注意它后面 the help of… 仍是 requires 的并列宾语，不是新句子，所以补出「也需要」让中文逻辑连起来。"},{"en":"such as economists and operational research experts.","lit":"比如经济学家和运筹学专家。","role":"（举例性同位修饰）","note":"难点： operational research experts 是熟词僻义陷阱 operational research 不是「操作研究」，而是固定术语「运筹学」（OR），二战中发展起来的应用数学分支。考生若按字面译「操作性研究专家」即丢分。这里译「运筹学专家／运筹学家」才到位。"}]},{"n":32,"en":"Furthermore, it is obvious that the strength of a country's economy is directly bound up with the efficiency of its agriculture and industry, and that this in turn rests upon the efforts of scientists and technologists of all kinds.","refZh":"此外，显而易见的是，一个国家的经济实力与其农业和工业的效率直接紧密相连，而这一点反过来又取决于各类科学家和技术人员的努力。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Furthermore, it is obvious that","lit":"此外，显而易见的是","role":"（连接副词 + 形式主语 it + that 引导的真主语从句）","note":"难点： 形式主语 it 的处理 it is obvious that… 是「形式主语＋真主语从句」结构，it 不译，that 后面才是真正的主语内容。中文译为「显而易见的是」「显然」「不言而喻」均可。Furthermore 译「此外／而且」，承上启下。"},{"en":"the strength of a country's economy is directly bound up with the efficiency of its agriculture and industry,","lit":"一个国家的经济实力直接与其农业和工业的效率紧密相连，","role":"（第一个 that 宾语从句的主体）","note":"难点： be bound up with = 与…紧密相连 bound up with 是固定搭配，意为「与…密切相关／紧密相连」，不是「被绑起来」。directly 强调「直接地」，要译出来。its 指代 a country's，译「该国的」或承前省略均可。"},{"en":"and that this in turn rests upon the efforts of scientists and technologists of all kinds.","lit":"而这又反过来取决于各类科学家和技术人员的努力。","role":"（第二个 that 引导的并列宾语从句）","note":"难点： this 回指 + in turn + rest upon 三连难点 this 回指前一分句的「农业和工业的效率」（或整个「经济与农工业效率挂钩」这件事），可译「这一点／农工业的效率」；in turn 不是「轮流」，而是「反过来／进而」，表示递进的因果链；rest upon = depend on，「取决于／依赖于」。and that 中的 that 与前一 that 并列，都做 obvious 的真主语，不能漏。"}]},{"n":33,"en":"Owing to the remarkable development in mass-communications, people everywhere are feeling new wants and are being exposed to new customs and ideas, while governments are often forced to introduce still further innovations for the reasons given above.","refZh":"由于大众传播的显著发展，各地的人们都在产生新的需求，并接触到新的习俗与观念；与此同时，出于上述原因，政府也常常被迫推行更多的革新举措。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Owing to the remarkable development in mass-communications,","lit":"由于大众传播的显著发展，","role":"（原因状语）","note":"难点： Owing to = 由于；mass-communications = 大众传播 Owing to 等同于 due to／because of，译「由于／因为」。mass-communications 不是「大量交流」，是固定术语「大众传播／大众传媒」（指报刊、广播、电视等）。remarkable development 译「显著发展／巨大发展」均可。"},{"en":"people everywhere are feeling new wants","lit":"各地的人们都在产生新的需求","role":"（并列分句一：主谓宾）","note":"难点： wants 名词＝需求/欲望；feel new wants 译「产生新需求」 wants 在这里是名词复数（不是动词），意为「需求／欲望／渴求」（同 needs/desires）。feeling new wants 直译「感到新需求」生硬，汉化为「产生新的需求／感到有了新的需求」更顺。people everywhere 译「各地的人／世界各地的人们」。"},{"en":"and are being exposed to new customs and ideas,","lit":"并接触到新的习俗与观念，","role":"（并列分句一的并列谓语，被动语态）","note":"难点： be exposed to 被动转主动 be exposed to 字面是「被暴露给／被让接触」，汉化时不要直译被动，转主动「接触到／受到…的影响／开始了解」更地道。customs 在此是「风俗／习俗」，不是「海关」（熟词僻义反向陷阱）。"},{"en":"while governments are often forced to introduce still further innovations","lit":"与此同时，政府常常被迫推行更多的革新举措","role":"（对比并列分句二：while + 主谓）","note":"难点： while 表对比/同时；still further 表「更进一步」 while 在此不译「虽然」，而是「与此同时／而」，表两件事并行。be forced to 可译「被迫／不得不」。still further innovations 中 still 加强 further，意为「更进一步的／更多的」，innovations 译「革新／创新举措」。introduce 在此语境译「推行／引入」而非「介绍」。"},{"en":"for the reasons given above.","lit":"出于上述原因。","role":"（原因状语）","note":"难点： given above = 上述/前文所述 given above 是过去分词作 reasons 的后置定语，意为「上文给出的／上述」。整个短语译「出于上述原因／出于前文所述原因」即可，无需展开第一段具体内容。"}]},{"n":34,"en":"in the early industrialized countries of Europe the process of industrialization—with all the far-reaching changes in social patterns that followed—was spread over nearly a century, whereas nowadays a developing nation may undergo the same process in a decade or so.","refZh":"在欧洲早期实现工业化的国家，工业化进程——连同随之而来的社会形态的一切深远变化——延续了将近一个世纪；然而，如今一个发展中国家可能在十年左右就完成同样的进程。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"in the early industrialized countries of Europe","lit":"在欧洲早期实现工业化的国家","role":"（地点状语）","note":"难点： early industrialized 是定语，不要拆开 early industrialized countries 不是「早期国家」+「工业化的」，而是「早期实现工业化的国家」——early 修饰 industrialized，整体作 countries 的前置定语。译为「欧洲早期实现工业化的国家／欧洲早期工业化国家」。of Europe 译「欧洲的」。"},{"en":"the process of industrialization—with all the far-reaching changes in social patterns that followed—was spread over nearly a century,","lit":"工业化进程——连同随之而来的社会形态的一切深远变化——延续了将近一个世纪，","role":"（主句（主语 + 破折号插入语 + 被动谓语 + 时间状语））","note":"难点： 破折号插入语 + that followed 后置定语 + 被动转主动 本块结构是「主语 the process of industrialization —— 插入语 with…that followed —— 被动谓语 was spread over nearly a century」。三处难点：① 两个破折号之间是 with + N + that 定从的插入语，far-reaching 译「深远的」是采分关键词，social patterns 译「社会形态」，that followed 是修饰 changes（不是 social patterns），意为「随之而来的（变化）」；② was spread over a period 是固定表达「延续了／持续了某段时间」，不是「被铺开」，被动转主动；③ industrialization 全文统一译「工业化」，process 译「进程」。汉化时建议把插入语在中文里也用破折号或独立成短句保留，结构更清。"},{"en":"whereas nowadays a developing nation may undergo the same process in a decade or so.","lit":"然而如今一个发展中国家可能在十年左右就经历同样的进程。","role":"（对比并列分句）","note":"难点： whereas = 然而／而；undergo = 经历 whereas 是对比连词，译「然而／而」，表两边对照。undergo 译「经历／经受」。in a decade or so 译「十年左右／大约十年」。may 在此是「可能／也许」，表客观可能性。a developing nation 译「（一个）发展中国家」，nation 在此与 country 同义。"}]},{"n":35,"en":"Additional social stresses may also occur because of the population explosion or problems arising from mass migration movements—themselves made relatively easy nowadays by modern means of transport.","refZh":"另外的社会压力也可能出现，原因是人口爆炸，或者是由大规模移民运动引发的种种问题——而这种移民运动如今由于现代交通工具的发展已变得相对容易。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Additional social stresses may also occur","lit":"另外的社会压力也可能产生","role":"（主句主谓）","note":"难点： Additional = 额外的／另外的；stresses 是「压力」 Additional 译「额外的／另外的／更多的」；social stresses 译「社会压力／社会紧张」；may also occur 译「也可能出现／也可能产生」。注意 may 是「可能」，不是「可以」。"},{"en":"because of the population explosion","lit":"由于人口爆炸","role":"（原因状语 1）","note":"难点： population explosion 固定术语「人口爆炸」 因术语固定，直接译「人口爆炸」即可。because of 译「由于／因为」。"},{"en":"or problems arising from mass migration movements—themselves made relatively easy nowadays by modern means of transport.","lit":"或由大规模移民运动引发的问题——而这种移民运动如今因现代交通手段而变得相对容易。","role":"（原因状语 2（并列）+ 现在分词后置定语 + 破折号独立主格补充）","note":"难点： arising from 后置定语 + themselves 独立主格 + 被动转主动 三连难点 本块包含本句两个最硬的难点：① arising from 是现在分词作 problems 的后置定语，意为「由…引起／产生的」，汉化时前移译「由…引起的问题」；mass migration movements 译「大规模移民运动」。② 破折号后 themselves made relatively easy nowadays by modern means of transport 是「独立主格／非限定定从简化」结构，themselves 回指 mass migration movements，等价于 which are themselves made relatively easy…；汉化时把代词还原成「这种移民运动本身」，被动 made…easy by 转主动「因…而变得容易」。③ modern means of transport 译「现代交通工具／现代交通手段」。三处都是主体考生的盲区，缺一处就丢一片采分点。"}]}]},{"id":"section3","kind":"writing","title":"Section III 写作","directions":"36. Directions: A. Study the following two pictures carefully and write an essay of at least 150 words. B. Your essay must be written neatly on ANSWER SHEET 2. C. Your essay should meet the requirements below: 1）Describe the pictures. 2）Deduce the purpose of the painter of the pictures. 3）Suggest counter-measures.","prompt":"36. Directions: A. Study the following two pictures carefully and write an essay of at least 150 words. B. Your essay must be written neatly on ANSWER SHEET 2. C. Your essay should meet the requirements below: 1）Describe the pictures. 2）Deduce the purpose of the painter of the pictures. 3）Suggest counter-measures.","points":10,"image":{"src":"assets/writing/2000-section3.jpg","alt":"这幅图像描绘了一幅名为“A Brief History of World Commercial Fishing”的视觉比较","width":"911","height":"815","local":"assets/writing/2000-section3.jpg"},"model":{"essay":"The two pictures present a striking contrast under the shared title \"A Brief History of World Commercial Fishing.\" In the first one, dated 1900, only a couple of small boats float on a sea teeming with fish. In the second, marked 1995, the boats have multiplied into a crowded fleet, yet the fish beneath them have dwindled to a mere handful. What the painter intends to convey is far from a simple record of the fishing industry. Through this sharp before-and-after comparison, the artist warns us of the alarming depletion of marine resources caused by unchecked overfishing. As human greed and advanced technology drive more and more vessels into the ocean, the once-abundant fish population is being pushed to the edge of exhaustion. The message is clear: if we keep taking from nature without restraint, we will eventually be left with empty nets and a dead sea. Effective counter-measures are therefore urgently needed. For one thing, governments should set strict fishing quotas and enforce closed seasons so that fish stocks have time to recover. For another, individuals ought to consume seafood responsibly and support sustainable fisheries. Only when awareness, regulation and action work together can we protect the ocean and pass on a living blue planet to future generations.","translation":"这两幅图以共同的标题“世界商业捕鱼简史”呈现出鲜明的对比。第一幅标注为 1900 年，海面上只漂着寥寥几条小船，海里却鱼群密布。第二幅标注为 1995 年，渔船已增至一支拥挤的船队，船下的鱼却只剩下屈指可数的几条。\n画家想要传达的，远不止是对渔业的简单记录。通过这组鲜明的今昔对比，作者警示我们：无节制的过度捕捞正在造成海洋资源惊人的枯竭。当人类的贪婪与先进技术驱使越来越多的船只涌入海洋，曾经丰饶的鱼群正被逼到耗尽的边缘。寓意十分清楚：如果我们继续毫无节制地向自然索取，最终只会落得空网一场、海死鱼绝。\n因此，切实的对策已迫在眉睫。一方面，政府应设定严格的捕捞配额、推行休渔期，让鱼群有时间恢复。另一方面，个人应理性消费海产、支持可持续渔业。唯有当意识、监管与行动共同发力，我们才能守护海洋，把一个仍有生机的蓝色星球留给后代。","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"对比总起＋两句反差","text":"【第 1 段】 对比总起＋两句反差 。首段用 present a striking contrast 一句总起，再以 In the first one, dated 1900 和 In the second, marked 1995 两句写船鱼此消彼长，落实『点对比、不流水账』，只三句就交代完 Describe the pictures，不拖泥带水。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"过渡＋点破＋加重","text":"【第 2 段】 过渡＋点破＋加重 。第二段用 far from a simple record 自然过渡，再以 warns us of the alarming depletion of marine resources 点破画家用意，末句 if we keep... we will eventually 用假设加重语气，完成 Deduce the purpose of the painter of the pictures，寓意紧扣上段画面。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"两级对策＋升华","text":"【第 3 段】 两级对策＋升华 。末段用 For one thing / For another 把对策分派给 governments 与 individuals，各带一个可操作动作，最后 Only when... can we 升华收尾，落实『对策落到具体主体』，回应 Suggest counter-measures。"}],"wordCount":209}}],"questionCount":30,"objectiveCount":30,"answerTable":{"ans-section1":"完形填空（四选一） Section I （1–10 题） 1 C instead of · 2 A only if · 3 B against · 4 A replace · 5 C feed · 6 D channels · 7 B self-sufficient · 8 D seek · 9 C rate · 10 D frequently \n（逐题解析见 完形填空（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-1":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (1) （11–14 题） 11 C · 12 D · 13 B · 14 A \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-2":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (2) （15–18 题） 15 C · 16 B · 17 A · 18 D \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-3":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (3) （19–22 题） 19 B · 20 A · 21 C · 22 D \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-4":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (4) （23–26 题） 23 B · 24 D · 25 C · 26 A \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-5":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (5) （27–30 题） 27 A · 28 C · 29 D · 30 B \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-b":"英译汉（划线句子翻译） Section II Part B \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 英译汉（划线句子翻译）解析页","ans-section3":"写作 Section III \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页"},"coverage":{"objective":30,"explained":30,"missingSections":[]}};
